# Keep methods exposed to JavaScript through the gin Java bridge
# (JavascriptInjector.addPossiblyUnsafeInterface with the
# android.webkit.JavascriptInterface annotation). The bridge resolves each
# exposed method by its Java name at runtime via reflection, so R8 must not
# rename or strip these methods or the JS-visible name disappears. Without this,
# window.BravePiPNavigator.restorePipOriginTab() (see
# BraveYouTubeScriptInjectorNativeHelper.PiPTabRestorer) is undefined in release
# (minified) builds and YouTube PiP tab restore silently no-ops, even though it
# works in unminified debug builds.
-keepclasseswithmembers,includedescriptorclasses class * {
    @android.webkit.JavascriptInterface <methods>;
}
